{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And the reason for <b>if no man has lain with you and if you have not gone astray in impurity</b> — these two conditions are one. That is: if no man has lain with you, meaning you have not gone astray in impurity under your husband — you are innocent, for her husband has lain with her and he is a man. And it is possible that אִישׁ is indefinite (lacking the definite article), meaning: if the man has not lain with you and if you have not gone astray in impurity under your husband at all, for he administers the oath to her concerning that specific man regarding whom he was explicitly jealous, and concerning others by implication. And so they said (Sotah 18a): \"Amen from this man, and Amen from another man.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:53.631359717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}